        "analysis_json": "{\"verdict\": \"Passenger\", \"summary\": \"PASSENGER. Gazlowe failed to establish fundamental lane presence, generating **0 Pure Soak** which severely limited the team's ambient experience generation, a critical misstep for a hero capable of high lane control. Although Gazlowe secured **3 personal mercenary captures**, these efforts did not adequately compensate for the absence of passive minion experience, particularly in conjunction with only **1 Tribute** objective participation. This macro inefficiency prevented the team from fully leveraging their early Level 10 and Level 20 power spikes, ultimately contributing to the loss despite having talent advantages.\", \"key_insights\": {\"mercenary_camps\": 3, \"downtime\": \"0:22\"}, \"critical_mistake\": \"Gazlowe's complete absence from lane soaking, evidenced by **0 Pure Soak**, represented a critical macro failure. This prevented the team from accumulating vital passive experience, weakening their ability to sustain map pressure and convert Level 10 and Level 20 advantages into tangible structural gains.\", \"win_condition\": \"The team achieved a critical Level 10 power advantage at 7:15, 68 seconds before the enemy team, securing the ultimate tier. Despite later reaching Level 20 at 15:38 while the enemy never did, the team failed to convert these talent advantages into a decisive victory due to persistent macro-economic inefficiencies and objective control failures.\", \"tactical_breakdown\": \"Gazlowe's single death, recorded as an outnumbered death, indicates a positional error or a late rotation into a collapsing teamfight. Gazlowe's participation in only **1 Tribute** throughout the game contributed to the team's objective deficit, as the enemy secured twice as many Tributes (4 to 2), granting them map control and ultimately the Curse that decided the game.\"}",
